    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d276">

                <pb facs="0654" n="534" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg534"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">885.73/151: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Riddle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-07-01T19:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 1, 1922—7
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 2—12:05
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>40. Your no. 25, June 28, 6 p.m.<anchor n="63" xml:id="d276-f1"/> Minister of the
                    Interior and Procurador del Tesoro Lopez assured me today that they would favor
                    granting permission to any American cable company to lay a cable to Brazil, and
                    they felt sure that Argentine Government could have no objection; but that
                    administrative measures to make this binding would probably require six weeks to
                    two months although no congressional action is necessary. Lopez stated that in
                    his opinion article 13 was a precarious concession<anchor n="64"
                        xml:id="d276-f2"/> for the reason that no term was specified and could
                    therefore be rescinded by Congress, and that article 17 would not prove bar to
                    the laying of a cable by any company.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Riddle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d276-f1" n="63" xml:id="d276-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d276-f2" n="64" xml:id="d276-f2-content">
                <p>i.e., the privilege was held during the pleasure of the grantor.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
